Until a run reach a terminal state 'expired  | completed | failed | incomplete | cancelled ' the current thread is locked and no messages can be added to it.  Calling `stop` is not guaranteed to cancel a run - it just aborts the in-flight fetch - so the thread can remain locked until it times out.   There is a separate openai [cancelRun](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/runs/cancelRun) end point to cancel a run,this also is [not guaranteed to cancel](https://platform.openai.com/docs/assistants/how-it-works/runs-and-run-steps) ... but so far it has worked for me - but I don't know how to trap if it fails.  My hacked together solution was to 1) capture the current run id  when creating a new stream, and then have a new DELETE route on my \api\assistant.  e.g.

```ts
